Personal Experiences

Maria, 34 – Flu
“I got the flu last winter and it honestly knocked me out more than I expected. It started with just feeling tired and a little cold, but by the next day I had a fever and my whole body ached. I remember not even wanting to get out of bed because everything felt heavy. What really helped me was just slowing down and letting my body rest, even though I felt like I was wasting time. I drank a lot of water and some soup, even when I didnt have much of an appetite. I also stayed home from work for a few days because I didnt want to get my coworkers sick. After about 3 or 4 days the fever went down, but I still felt weak for a while after. It kinda reminded me that pushing through being sick isnt always the best idea.”
