Tanya, 42 – COVID-19
“When I tested positive for COVID-19, I was honestly nervous because I had heard so many different stories from people. For me, it started with a mild cough and feeling really tired, but then I noticed I couldnt smell or taste anything which was kinda scary. I made sure to stay isolated in my room so I didnt spread it to my family. If I had to come out, I wore a mask and wiped down things I touched. I kept checking my temperature and tried to rest as much as possible. Drinking warm drinks helped a little with the cough. It took about a week before I started feeling better, but even after that I didnt feel fully normal for a bit. That whole experience made me take sickness more seriously than before.”
