Luis, 28 – Common Cold
“I get the common cold probably more than I should, and over time I’ve kinda figured out what works for me. Usually it starts with a sore throat and runny nose, then I just feel kinda off for a few days. Its not super serious but it still slows me down a lot. I try to drink hot tea, especially at night, and get more sleep than usual. One thing I try to be more aware of now is not being too close to people when I know Im getting sick, because its easy to pass it on without thinking. I also wash my hands more often during that time. It usually clears up in a few days, but I try not to ignore it because it can still affect other people.”

